### IBM i (The Order Book): what the game adds to the 5250 session, which
### has no function keys. Panels and system messages stay in English, like
### the system.

# A long list: the lines left out between its first and its last ones. { $count }: how many.
ibmi-skipped = {"  "}… { $count } more lines (on a real 5250 screen: Page Down) …
# Under DSPMSG, when an inquiry waits for a reply.
ibmi-reply-tip = Type the reply (one of the values in parentheses), ? to read the message's help (F1 on a real screen), or press Enter to leave it unanswered.
# After signing on.
ibmi-signon-tip = Type CL commands at ===> (WRKACTJOB, DSPMSG QSYSOPR…). CMD ? shows a command's help (F1/F4 on a real screen). SIGNOFF, or 90, closes the session.
# A menu number other than 90.
ibmi-menu-option = The menus aren't simulated: type CL commands at ===> (WRKACTJOB, DSPMSG QSYSOPR, WRKSPLF…), or SIGNOFF to leave.
